---
title: webserv — CGI lifecycle (CgiHandler is a STUB today)
---

%%{init: {"theme": "dark"}}%%

%% =====================================================================
%% CGI = Common Gateway Interface (RFC 3875).
%% It's the original way a web server lets a script generate a response.
%%
%% Today's status: src/cgi/CgiHandler.cpp is a stub.
%% start() sets state = FAILED and returns false, so nothing breaks but
%% nothing works. The shape below is what the IMPLEMENTATION will look
%% like once it's wired up.
%%
%% Why CGI is special here:
%%   • fork() is forbidden by the subject EXCEPT for CGI. This is the
%%     only file in webserv that may call fork().
%%   • The child's stdin/stdout become PIPES. Those pipe fds are
%%     non-blocking and live in the SAME poll() loop as the client
%%     sockets — webserv doesn't get a second event loop.
%%   • waitpid() must use WNOHANG. A blocking waitpid would freeze the
%%     server while one CGI script runs.
%% =====================================================================

flowchart TB

    %% ── What CGI is, in plain English ────────────────────────────
    subgraph WHAT["What CGI is, in plain English"]
        direction TB
        what1["Request comes in:<br/>GET /cgi-bin/hello.py?name=sedat HTTP/1.1"]
        what2["webserv decides ‘.py = CGI’,<br/>so instead of reading a file,<br/>it RUNS a program."]
        what3["The child program (python3, php-cgi, ...)<br/>reads request info from env vars,<br/>reads the request body from its stdin,<br/>and writes its response to its stdout."]
        what4["webserv collects that stdout,<br/>parses it into an HttpResponse,<br/>and sends it back to the browser."]
        what1 --> what2 --> what3 --> what4
    end

    %% ── The wire format the child writes ─────────────────────────
    subgraph WIRE["What the child writes to its stdout"]
        direction TB
        wire1["Content-Type: text/html  CRLF<br/>Status: 200 OK  CRLF        (optional, default 200)<br/>CRLF        (blank line — end of headers)<br/>&lt;html&gt;Hello, sedat&lt;/html&gt;"]
        wire2["Headers, blank line, body —<br/>just like HTTP without the request line.<br/>If there's no Content-Length, the body<br/>ends at EOF on the stdout pipe."]
        wire1 --> wire2
    end

    %% ── The state machine ────────────────────────────────────────
    subgraph STATES["CgiHandler state machine"]
        direction TB

        s0(["INIT<br/>just constructed,<br/>no process yet"]):::s_init
        s1(["SPAWNED<br/>pipe + fork + execve OK<br/>parent owns stdin/stdout pipe fds,<br/>both non-blocking,<br/>both registered with Server's poll"]):::s_ok
        s2(["SENDING_STDIN<br/>writing request body into<br/>child's stdin pipe,<br/>bytes_sent offset pattern<br/>(same idea as Connection.bytesSent)"]):::s_ok
        s3(["READING_STDOUT<br/>reading child's stdout into<br/>_rawOutput buffer"]):::s_ok
        s4(["DONE<br/>BOTH conditions met:<br/>• stdout hit EOF (read == 0)<br/>• waitpid(WNOHANG) reaped the child<br/>_rawOutput is ready to parse"]):::s_done
        s5(["FAILED<br/>pipe/fork/exec error,<br/>OR write/read returned ≤ 0,<br/>OR timeout (> 10 s) → kill SIGKILL.<br/>_rawOutput holds a canned 500 body"]):::s_err

        s0 -- "start():<br/>pipe(toChild) + pipe(fromChild)<br/>fork() + (in child) execve()<br/>chdir(dirname(scriptPath))" --> s1
        s1 -- "body is empty (GET)" --> s3
        s1 -- "body present (POST)" --> s2
        s2 -- "onStdinWritable():<br/>all body bytes written →<br/>close stdinFd (EOF signal to child)" --> s3
        s3 -- "onStdoutReadable():<br/>read == 0 (child closed stdout)<br/>AND tick() already reaped the pid" --> s4

        s0 -. "pipe / fork / dup2 failed" .-> s5
        s2 -. "write returned ≤ 0" .-> s5
        s3 -. "read returned &lt; 0" .-> s5
        s1 -. "tick(): now - startTime > 10 s<br/>→ kill(pid, SIGKILL)" .-> s5
        s2 -. "same timeout path" .-> s5
        s3 -. "same timeout path" .-> s5
    end

    %% ── How Server will drive it ─────────────────────────────────
    subgraph WIRING["How Server will drive this (planned integration)"]
        direction TB
        wi1["1. Router decides a URL is CGI<br/>(URI matches a configured extension).<br/>It allocates CgiHandler*, calls start()."]
        wi2["2. Server keeps a<br/>std::map&lt;int, CgiHandler*&gt; _cgiByFd<br/>so each pipe fd maps back to its handler.<br/>Adds stdinFd (POLLOUT) and stdoutFd (POLLIN)<br/>to the SAME _fds vector as client sockets."]
        wi3["3. In Server::run() dispatch:<br/>if fd is in _cgiByFd → call<br/>onStdinWritable / onStdoutReadable.<br/>Each iteration also calls tick() on every<br/>active CGI (non-blocking waitpid + timeout)."]
        wi4["4. When isDone() or isFailed():<br/>parse _rawOutput into an HttpResponse<br/>on the owning Connection.<br/>Flip Connection to WRITING_RESPONSE.<br/>Remove pipe fds from poll, close them,<br/>delete the CgiHandler*."]
        wi1 --> wi2 --> wi3 --> wi4
    end

    %% ── Environment passed to the child ──────────────────────────
    subgraph ENV["CGI/1.1 env vars the router will build"]
        direction TB
        env1["REQUEST_METHOD   = GET / POST / DELETE<br/>QUERY_STRING     = stuff after '?'<br/>CONTENT_LENGTH   = body size (POST)<br/>CONTENT_TYPE     = request Content-Type<br/>SCRIPT_NAME      = /cgi-bin/hello.py<br/>SCRIPT_FILENAME  = absolute path<br/>PATH_INFO        = extra path after script<br/>SERVER_PROTOCOL  = HTTP/1.1<br/>SERVER_NAME / SERVER_PORT<br/>SERVER_SOFTWARE  = webserv/0.1<br/>GATEWAY_INTERFACE = CGI/1.1<br/>REMOTE_ADDR      = client IP<br/>HTTP_*           = every request header,<br/>                   upper-cased, '-' → '_'"]
    end

    %% ── Subject rules specific to CGI ────────────────────────────
    subgraph RULES["CGI-specific subject rules — grade-0 if broken"]
        direction TB
        r1["• fork() ONLY here — nowhere else."]
        r2["• Both pipe fds non-blocking,<br/>  driven by the SAME poll() loop.<br/>  Never read/write without poll readiness."]
        r3["• Never inspect errno after read/write<br/>  (no EAGAIN retry logic)."]
        r4["• waitpid MUST use WNOHANG —<br/>  blocking waitpid would freeze the server."]
        r5["• Chunked bodies must already be un-chunked<br/>  before being written to the child's stdin.<br/>  HttpRequest does this for us in BODY_CHUNKED."]
        r6["• If the child gives no Content-Length,<br/>  EOF on the stdout pipe = end of body.<br/>  Treat it as a normal termination."]
        r7["• Child must run with cwd = script's directory<br/>  (chdir before execve), so relative file<br/>  access inside the script works."]
    end

    classDef s_init  fill:#1a1a3a,stroke:#7c5cfc,color:#cba6ff
    classDef s_ok    fill:#13301e,stroke:#33aa66,color:#aaffcc
    classDef s_done  fill:#0e1a3a,stroke:#33aaff,color:#aaccff
    classDef s_err   fill:#3a1a1a,stroke:#cc6633,color:#ffccaa
